fix(proxy/bridge): editor Loading root causes found in field testing

Field testing (user able to open projects) exposed three deeper defects:

1. window.WebSocket wrapper dropped the native static constants
   (CONNECTING/OPEN/CLOSING/CLOSED). Overleaf's connection manager compares
   connection state against WebSocket.OPEN before creating a socket; both
   sides were undefined so canReconnect() stayed false forever and the
   editor never left its Loading screen. The wrapper now inherits the
   native prototype and statics (also keeping instanceof semantics).

2. Stored-credential authority silently dropped edge/load-balancer affinity
   cookies (gclb etc.) that the socket.io handshake ROTATES. The subsequent
   WebSocket upgrade then landed on a different backend and returned 502,
   leaving the editor on Loading (matches the intermittent 502 observed in
   field diagnostics). Routing cookies now keep the live browser value while
   application-session cookies stay stored-authoritative
   (mergeProxyCookieHeaders).

3. applyRuntimeConfig rebuilt the ReverseProxy without preserving the
   companion WS tunnel port/origin, so saving any setting silently removed
   the editor's dynamic WebSocket route.

Plus: bridge writes live diagnostics to <html data-dsh-overleaf-*> (ready /
ws-port / ws-target / ws-state / last-error / last-rejection).

Version 0.2.7 (codex field fix, reviewed and validated: build + both smoke
suites green + reinstalled into the web profile).
